issue_context.body:
Hello.
I have a problem to use private key which is loaded using OpenSSL v3.0.12 engine.
It works well in previous versions including v3.0.11.
Below are error logs.

```
[RSA]
4076AAB67F000000:error:020000B3:rsa routines:rsa_ossl_private_encrypt:missing private key:../openssl-3.0.12/crypto/rsa/rsa_ossl.c:332:
4076AAB67F000000:error:1C880004:Provider routines:rsa_sign:RSA lib:../openssl-3.0.12/providers/implementations/signature/rsa_sig.c:588:
4076AAB67F000000:error:06880006:asn1 encoding routines:ASN1_item_sign_ctx:EVP lib:../openssl-3.0.12/crypto/asn1/a_sign.c:284:
[EC]
40E63E917F000000:error:0800007D:elliptic curve routines:ossl_ecdsa_simple_sign_sig:missing private key:../openssl-3.0.12/crypto/ec/ecdsa_ossl.c:225:
40E63E917F000000:error:06880006:asn1 encoding routines:ASN1_item_sign_ctx:EVP lib:../openssl-3.0.12/crypto/asn1/a_sign.c:284:
```

Follow commit causes the problem.
https://github.com/openssl/openssl/commit/2b74e75331a27fc89cad9c8ea6a26c70019300b5

```e->load_privkey()``` sets engine specific evp methods.
```EVP_PKEY_set1_RSA``` (introduced by above commit) calls ```EVP_PKEY_assign``` and ```EVP_PKEY_set_type```.

``` 
EVP_PKEY *ENGINE_load_private_key(ENGINE *e, const char *key_id,
                                  UI_METHOD *ui_method, void *callback_data)
{
 EVP_PKEY *pkey;
 ...
    // [Reporter] Engine sets its own EVP method which should be called instead of default OpenSSL EVP method
    pkey = e->load_privkey(e, key_id, ui_method, callback_data);
    ...
    /* We enforce check for legacy key */
    switch (EVP_PKEY_get_id(pkey)) {
    case EVP_PKEY_RSA:
        {
        RSA *rsa = EVP_PKEY_get1_RSA(pkey);
        // [Reporter] By calling below, pkey loses its EVP engine information
        EVP_PKEY_set1_RSA(pkey, rsa);		//  [Reporter] Causes problem
        RSA_free(rsa);
        }
        break;
 ...
```
 
Within ```pkey_set_type```, information about EVP methods provided by the engine is invalidated, that is, can't access (call) engine specific EVP methods.
 
```
static int pkey_set_type(EVP_PKEY *pkey, ENGINE *e, int type, const char *str,
                         int len, EVP_KEYMGMT *keymgmt)
{
	...
	// At here, pmeth_engine is reset to NULL
	# ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE
        /* If we have ENGINEs release them */
        ENGINE_finish(pkey->engine);
        pkey->engine = NULL;
        ENGINE_finish(pkey->pmeth_engine);
        pkey->pmeth_engine = NULL;
	# endif
	...
 
```
 
```EVP_DigestSignInit```
-> ```do_sigver_init```
-> ```EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey```
-> ```int_ctx_new```
 
In above example ```pkey->pmeth_engine``` is null, so ```int_ctx_new``` calls OpenSSL default EVP methods.
Because default EVP methods can't handle engine specific pkey, it results in failure.
 
We fully understand that provider is recommend instead of engine, but there still exists various S/W components which use engine.
So kindly address above issue.
